KNOWNBUG
member.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member function template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
no body for callee
--
N5008 [dcl.fct.default]/4, [temp.mem]/1, [dcl.fct]/5 (default arguments are
not part of the parameter-type-list): the default on the in-class
declaration of S::m made the declaration's and the definition's parameter
lists compare unequal (cpp_typecheckt::member_template_parameters_match),
so the definition's body was never attached ("no body for callee").
Ignoring the default arguments there, and carrying them to the grafted
definition, fixes this test but attaches libstdc++'s
path::generic_string(const _Allocator & = _Allocator()) body, whose
`allocator_traits<_Allocator>::template rebind_alloc<value_type>' then
fails ("symbol 'value_type' is unknown"; the shape with std::allocator_traits
and a member typedef value_type, not reproduced header-free yet) and
cpp17_filesystem_basic / cpp17_filesystem_path_ops lose
generic_string and __str_codecvt_in.  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept this program (-std=c++98), and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
